Description: Wild OS: change a wallet's PAM key without a dialog
 pam_kwallet opens the wallet with a key made from the sign-in password,
 but does nothing when the password changes, so after a change the wallet
 never opens at sign-in again and the first app that needs a secret gets
 a prompt for the old password. kwalletd's own changePassword always shows
 a dialog. pamChangeHash re-encrypts the wallet from the key made from the
 old password to the key made from the new one, both made the way
 pam_kwallet makes them, and refuses if the old key does not open it.
 Wild OS Settings calls it after changing the account's password.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

